        {
            "source_entity_instance": "extreme winters of 2014 and 2015",
            "source_entity_type": "Weather_Event",
            "relation": "IMPACTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Subpolar Gyre",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "The extreme winters of 2014 and 2015 appear as key drivers of those recent and upcoming changes in the SPG. They are found to be responsible for rapidly cooling the upper ocean while feeding a 5-year delayed intensification of the overturning through increased light-to-dense transformation, leading eventually to a sharp warming of the domain.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "OSNAP array",
            "source_entity_type": "Instrument",
            "relation": "MEASURES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "circulation changes",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "Finally, the present analysis confirms the suitability of the international mooring-based OSNAP array for capturing the bulk of interannual and decadal circulation changes driven by air-sea buoyancy exchanges in the whole subpolar area.",
